{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model forecasts are systematically below realized prices across most horizons (roughly +2 to +8 EUR/t), especially during rising regimes.",
    "Trend/acceleration underreaction: when the last 1–2 weeks show a strong upswing, the model lags the move (too flat/slow). Apply an upward adjustment proportional to recent momentum (e.g., 5–10 day slope).",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: underprediction grows with horizon up to ~day 20–25 (largest gap mid-horizon), then narrows as the true series mean-reverts. Use a hump-shaped correction (bigger uplift mid-horizon, smaller at the end).",
    "Peak/plateau miss: during sustained rallies the model predicts a local peak/sideways action too early; shift the forecast path upward and slightly later (delay turning points).",
    "Late-horizon overhang after regime shift: when the true market rolls over (as in Example 5 tail), the model remains too high relative to the declining realized path. Add a conditional downward correction in the last ~5–10 days if recent realized prices start falling (negative short-term momentum)."
  ]
}
